WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.920
In the reign of Emperor Shenzong of Song, the brilliant Su Shi wrote many moving poems by candlelight.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:15.446
His poems circulated widely at court, and the officials whispered to one another, discussing them endlessly.

00:00:15.796 --> 00:00:20.092
But some frowned, with other plans in their hearts.

00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:29.106
Someone presented his verses to the emperor and accused Su Shi of satirizing the court; the mood in the hall instantly grew tense.

00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:35.936
Officers came to Su Shi's home and took him away for questioning; Su Shi's expression stayed calm.

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:40.150
The neighbors stood at the doorway, watching him with worry.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:48.372
In the courtroom, the officials took turns questioning the meaning of the poems, and Su Shi answered calmly.

00:00:48.722 --> 00:00:57.650
Su Shi set out on the road of exile, walking alone in the dusk — yet his poetry shines with undying light for later generations.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.720
When later generations read his poems, they are still deeply moved.

